# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained by design and
# will never get a fixed version. Nothing in this module's build graph
# imports the openpgp subpackage ("go mod why golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp"
# answers "main module does not need package"); x/crypto itself rides at the
# latest release only as a transitive module requirement. Suppressed rather
# than chased because no upgrade can clear a no-fix advisory on an unused
# subpackage.
GO-2026-5932

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2: the advisory states "This only affects your application
# if you are using the unstable RSC APIs". web/ is a client-only SPA: it imports
# BrowserRouter, MemoryRouter, Routes, Route, Navigate, NavLink, Outlet, Link,
# and useParams, and defines no loaders, actions, or server runtime, so the
# vulnerable action path never runs. There is also no upgrade that clears it
# here: the fix lands in react-router 8.3.0, but react-router-dom has no 8.x
# release ("npm view react-router-dom dist-tags" answers latest 7.18.2) and
# pins react-router to its own version. Revisit when react-router-dom ships an
# 8.x line. The four advisories that did apply (CVE-2026-55685, CVE-2026-53666,
# CVE-2026-53667, CVE-2026-53669) are cleared by the 7.18.2 bump.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
